# Normalize line endings repo-wide.
#
# Several checks in this repo compare freshly generated LF text against a
# committed artifact byte-for-byte, or hash a source file's exact bytes: the PRP
# contract manifest, the generated schema bundle, the semantic action catalog,
# and the replay goldens under packages/paperclip-runner. On a Windows clone
# with core.autocrlf=true those files check out as CRLF, so every `--check`
# script reports a stale artifact even when nothing changed, which blocks the
# runner build and the server typecheck that depends on it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git keep detecting binary files and leave them alone;
# `eol=lf` pins the working-tree copy of everything it does treat as text.
* text=auto eol=lf
